# ── SysMLv2 Integration Scheme (RH ruling 2026-07-25) ───────────────────────────
# SysMLv2 is IN-SCOPE EXTERNAL (the BFO/CCO posture: never managed nor extended
# by us, leveraged extensively). Written "SysMLv2" by convention (per the OMG MBSE
# wiki's usage, without the space). The language builds normatively on the KerML
# kernel, so the scheme dct:requires a KerML scheme — the Energistics-common
# dependency spine: each external advances its own versions, we adapt selectively.
#
# Like Energistics (and unlike FIBO/FHIR), OMG publishes no canonical RDF concept
# IRIs for SysMLv2 — mapping is at STANDARD grain (rdfs:seeAlso the OMG spec
# pages) and the spec_mappings module (sdg:Sysml* mapped entities) carries the
# entity-level evidence. seeAlso, never closeMatch (RH 2026-07-25).
#
# Sector entry (RH-ratified shape): sdg:Engineering at the sector tier
# (natural-cased tier-mate of FinancialSector/Healthcare/HeavyIndustries, member
# of sdg:TopicDomains + typed sdg:TopicDomain — instantiation, never a broader
# link) → sdg:MBSE as the ALL-CAPS genus chord (18.1) → sdg:SYSML re-homed
# beneath it (prefLabel "SysMLv2"), chord-VISIBLE, never a point. MBSE itself is
# ENUMERATED into the admission surface (aperture_include) and delta-gated like
# FINTECH/BIOTECH before it. THE LANGUAGE REPRESENTS; THE ONTOLOGY GROUNDS (RH
# 2026-07-25): manufacturing-domain concepts are NOT members of this scheme —
# they are domain-specific elements representable ATOP SysMLv2, grounded in
# their own sector (sdg:Manufacturing); the representability evidence lives in
# spec_mappings, never in scheme membership. Only genuine language concepts
# (the SYSML family) belong here.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dct:  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix sdg:  <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg#> .

# TopQuadrant thin-subclass pattern (mirrors sdg:FIBOConcept / sdg:FHIRConcept /
# sdg:EnergisticsConcept): the attachment point for governance annotations.
sdg:SysMLv2Concept rdfs:subClassOf skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "SysMLv2-aligned Concept" ;
    skos:definition "A curated SDG concept aligned to the OMG SysMLv2 language (atop the KerML kernel); carries SDG governance annotations while the standard remains external and authoritative." .

# ── the kernel + the language scheme ────────────────────────────────────────────

sdg:KerMLScheme a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "KerML Scheme" ;
    dct:hasVersion "1.0" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:definition "The OMG Kernel Modeling Language — the semantic kernel SysMLv2 builds on." .

sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme a skos:ConceptScheme ;
    rdfs:label "SysMLv2 Integration Scheme" ;
    dct:hasVersion "2.0" ;
    dct:requires sdg:KerMLScheme ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ,
        <https://www.omgwiki.org/MBSE/doku.php?id=mbse:sysml_v2_transition> ;
    skos:definition "Curated entry point into SysMLv2-aligned model-based systems engineering concepts within Signals Data Governance." ;
    skos:editorialNote "Version watch: the SysML v1→v2 transition is ongoing across the tool ecosystem (see the OMG MBSE wiki transition page); mappings pin to the v2 formal specification and adapt selectively as it revises." ;
    skos:hasTopConcept sdg:SYSML .

# ── the sector tier (RH 2026-07-25: sdg:Engineering, natural-cased tier-mate of
# FinancialSector/Healthcare/HeavyIndustries — a FOREST TOP; topic-domain-hood is
# INSTANTIATION via the sdg:TopicDomain class + sdg:TopicDomains membership, both
# declared in fibo_integration.ttl, never a broader link) ───────────────────────

sdg:Engineering a skos:Concept, sdg:TopicDomain ;
    skos:prefLabel "Engineering" ;
    skos:altLabel "Engineering" ;
    skos:notation "18" ;
    skos:definition "The sector-tier top for engineering topic domains within SDG — initially hosting the model-based systems engineering genus (sdg:MBSE), organizing without admitting. Deliberately broader than any one language or standards body: SysMLv2 and KerML contribute through their integration schemes, and future engineering contributors join as siblings. A sector-tier forest top (a sdg:TopicDomain, member of sdg:TopicDomains) — no parent above it." ;
    skos:inScheme <https://signals.zndx.org/sdg/scheme> .

# ── the genus chord (admission anchor — ENUMERATED via aperture_include) ────────

sdg:MBSE a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Model-Based Systems Engineering" ;
    skos:altLabel "MBSE" , "SysMLv2-aligned Concepts" ;
    skos:notation "18.1" ;
    skos:definition "The practice domain where systems are specified, analyzed, and verified through coherent models rather than documents — the genus for SysMLv2-aligned modeling concepts within SDG." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Covers the modeled system across its engineering lifecycle — requirement definitions with satisfaction and verification traceability; structural decomposition into parts, ports, and connection usages; behavioral modeling of actions, states, and sequence-structured occurrences; parametric constraints; and verification cases binding requirements to analysis, inspection, and test evidence. Terminology traces to the OMG SysMLv2 language atop the KerML kernel — the methodology axis: manufacturing and other domain semantics are represented atop it as domain-specific elements, grounded in their own sectors." ;
    skos:broader sdg:Engineering ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

# ── multi-scheme memberships (many-to-many lattice; membership shift, never
# re-rooting). The concepts stay DECLARED in domain_concepts.ttl (their home);
# these assertions add standard-scheme membership only. LANGUAGE concepts only —
# the former MFG memberships were the blend in miniature and were edited away
# (Scratch-edit doctrine) when the Manufacturing sector separated the axes. ─────

sdg:SYSML a sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:topConceptOf sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .
sdg:SYSML_REQUIREMENTS a sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .
sdg:SYSML_STRUCTURE a sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .
sdg:SYSML_BEHAVIOR a sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .
sdg:SYSML_VERIFICATION a sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

# ── the CONTROLLED-VOCABULARY tier (task #44 increment (a), RH's DDL yardstick
# 2026-07-25): the SKOS SOURCE for the semantic layer's reference tables.
# TRIAD BY GENERATION: kvasir's scheme→lookup lowering will emit
# sysml_metaclasses / sysml_relationship_kinds DDL + seed rows FROM these
# members (Collection = table, member = row; spec_ref/sdg_concept_iri columns
# carry rdfs:seeAlso + these IRIs).
#
# CENSUS-VERIFIED (2026-07-25) against the OFFICIAL metamodel —
# Systems-Modeling/SysML-v2-Pilot-Implementation org.omg.sysml/model/SysML.ecore
# (182 EClasses; artifact: build/foreign/sysmlv2/census_30.json). Every abstract
# flag and every specialization link below is READ FROM the metamodel, never
# folklore (the census corrected three wrong abstract flags on first run, and
# caught that Allocation/Connection/ItemFlow are NOT metaclasses — the language
# reifies them as AllocationUsage/ConnectionUsage/Flow-family usages; those
# three rows are SDG RELATIONAL FLATTENINGS, marked as such). In-set
# specializations are skos:broader; out-of-set supertypes are recorded in
# editorial notes without minting concepts (census discipline: confirmed links
# only, no scope creep). NEVER aperture points.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

sdg:SysMLv2Metaclasses a skos:Collection ;
    skos:prefLabel "SysMLv2 Metaclasses" ;
    skos:definition "The controlled vocabulary of KerML/SysMLv2 metaclasses used by the semantic layer's element backbone — the SKOS source of the sysml_metaclasses reference table. Census-verified against the official Ecore metamodel." ;
    skos:member sdg:SysMLv2_Element , sdg:SysMLv2_Namespace , sdg:SysMLv2_Relationship ,
        sdg:SysMLv2_Type , sdg:SysMLv2_Classifier , sdg:SysMLv2_Feature , sdg:SysMLv2_Class ,
        sdg:SysMLv2_PartDefinition , sdg:SysMLv2_PartUsage ,
        sdg:SysMLv2_ActionDefinition , sdg:SysMLv2_ActionUsage ,
        sdg:SysMLv2_RequirementDefinition , sdg:SysMLv2_RequirementUsage ,
        sdg:SysMLv2_AllocationDefinition , sdg:SysMLv2_AllocationUsage ,
        sdg:SysMLv2_ConnectionDefinition ,
        sdg:SysMLv2_ItemDefinition , sdg:SysMLv2_ItemUsage ,
        sdg:SysMLv2_AttributeDefinition , sdg:SysMLv2_AttributeUsage .

sdg:SysMLv2RelationshipKinds a skos:Collection ;
    skos:prefLabel "SysMLv2 Relationship Kinds" ;
    skos:definition "The controlled vocabulary for the semantic layer's relations backbone — the SKOS source of the sysml_relationship_kinds reference table. Seven members are census-verified Relationship-family metaclasses; three (Allocation, Connection, ItemFlow) are SDG relational flattenings of constructs the language reifies as usages, marked as such per member." ;
    skos:member sdg:SysMLv2_OwningMembership , sdg:SysMLv2_FeatureMembership ,
        sdg:SysMLv2_Specialization , sdg:SysMLv2_Subsetting , sdg:SysMLv2_FeatureTyping ,
        sdg:SysMLv2_Succession , sdg:SysMLv2_Allocation , sdg:SysMLv2_Connection ,
        sdg:SysMLv2_ItemFlow , sdg:SysMLv2_Dependency .

# ── KerML-layer metaclasses (Root/Core/Kernel) — census-confirmed ──────────────

sdg:SysMLv2_Element a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Element" ;
    skos:definition "Root syntactic element of the KerML abstract syntax — the common supertype of everything in a model." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Root · ABSTRACT (census) · no supertype" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Namespace a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Namespace" ;
    skos:definition "An element that contains and names other elements via memberships." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Root · specializes (census): Element" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_Element ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Relationship a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Relationship" ;
    skos:definition "Reified relationship element relating source and target elements." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Root · ABSTRACT (census) · specializes (census): Element" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_Element ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Type a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Type" ;
    skos:definition "A namespace classifying things by conditions on membership — the root of the classification hierarchy." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Core · concrete (census corrected 2026-07-25: NOT abstract) · specializes (census): Namespace" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_Namespace ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Classifier a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Classifier" ;
    skos:definition "A type classifying instances directly." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Core · concrete (census corrected 2026-07-25: NOT abstract) · specializes (census): Type" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_Type ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Feature a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Feature" ;
    skos:definition "A type classifying how instances relate — the usage/role side of the type system." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Core · concrete (census corrected 2026-07-25: NOT abstract) · specializes (census): Type" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_Type ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Class a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Class" ;
    skos:definition "Kernel classifier of occurrences and objects." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Kernel · specializes (census): Classifier" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_Classifier ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

# ── Systems-layer metaclasses — census-confirmed ────────────────────────────────

sdg:SysMLv2_PartDefinition a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "PartDefinition" ;
    skos:definition "Definition of a class of systems or parts of systems." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): ItemDefinition — parts ARE items in SysMLv2" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_ItemDefinition ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_PartUsage a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "PartUsage" ;
    skos:definition "Usage of a part within a context — the Definition/Usage pattern's usage side for parts." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): ItemUsage" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_ItemUsage ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_ActionDefinition a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "ActionDefinition" ;
    skos:definition "Definition of a class of actions or processes." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): OccurrenceDefinition, Behavior (out-of-set — await census expansion)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:broader sdg:SYSML ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_ActionUsage a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "ActionUsage" ;
    skos:definition "Usage of an action within a behavior or process context." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): OccurrenceUsage, Step (out-of-set)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:broader sdg:SYSML ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_RequirementDefinition a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "RequirementDefinition" ;
    skos:definition "Definition of a requirement — a constraint that must be satisfied." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): ConstraintDefinition (out-of-set) — requirements ARE constraints in SysMLv2" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:broader sdg:SYSML ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_RequirementUsage a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "RequirementUsage" ;
    skos:definition "Usage of a requirement within a context." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): ConstraintUsage (out-of-set)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:broader sdg:SYSML ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_AllocationDefinition a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "AllocationDefinition" ;
    skos:definition "Definition of an allocation — a mapping of one model element onto another." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): ConnectionDefinition — allocations ARE connections in SysMLv2" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_ConnectionDefinition ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_AllocationUsage a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "AllocationUsage" ;
    skos:definition "Usage of an allocation within a context." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): ConnectionUsage (out-of-set)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:broader sdg:SYSML ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_ConnectionDefinition a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "ConnectionDefinition" ;
    skos:definition "Definition of a connection between parts." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): PartDefinition, AssociationStructure (2nd out-of-set) — connections ARE parts in SysMLv2" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_PartDefinition ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_ItemDefinition a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "ItemDefinition" ;
    skos:definition "Definition of a class of items — things flowing through or handled by a system." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): OccurrenceDefinition, Structure (out-of-set)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:broader sdg:SYSML ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_ItemUsage a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "ItemUsage" ;
    skos:definition "Usage of an item within a context." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): OccurrenceUsage (out-of-set)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:broader sdg:SYSML ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_AttributeDefinition a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "AttributeDefinition" ;
    skos:definition "Definition of an attribute — a data-valued feature." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): Definition, DataType (out-of-set)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:broader sdg:SYSML ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_AttributeUsage a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "AttributeUsage" ;
    skos:definition "Usage of an attribute within a context." ;
    skos:editorialNote "layer: Systems · specializes (census): Usage (out-of-set)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/SysML/> ;
    skos:broader sdg:SYSML ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

# ── relationship kinds — 7 census-verified metaclasses + 3 SDG flattenings ─────

sdg:SysMLv2_OwningMembership a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "OwningMembership" ;
    skos:definition "Ownership / containment membership — the relationship by which a namespace owns an element." ;
    skos:editorialNote "specializes (census): Membership (out-of-set)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_FeatureMembership a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "FeatureMembership" ;
    skos:definition "Membership of a feature in a type." ;
    skos:editorialNote "specializes (census): OwningMembership" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_OwningMembership ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Specialization a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Specialization" ;
    skos:definition "Generalization / specialization between types." ;
    skos:editorialNote "specializes (census): Relationship" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_Relationship ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Subsetting a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Subsetting" ;
    skos:definition "Subsetting between features — one feature's values are a subset of another's." ;
    skos:editorialNote "specializes (census): Specialization" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_Specialization ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_FeatureTyping a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "FeatureTyping" ;
    skos:definition "Typing of a feature by a classifier." ;
    skos:editorialNote "specializes (census): Specialization" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_Specialization ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Succession a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Succession" ;
    skos:definition "Temporal / sequential succession between occurrences — the ordering relationship process plans lower to operation sequences." ;
    skos:editorialNote "specializes (census): Connector (out-of-set)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Allocation a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Allocation" ;
    skos:definition "Allocation edge in the semantic layer's relations backbone — an SDG relational flattening of what SysMLv2 reifies as AllocationUsage (a connection usage, not an edge kind)." ;
    skos:editorialNote "SDG RELATIONAL FLATTENING (census 2026-07-25: NOT a SysMLv2 metaclass) — the reified form is sdg:SysMLv2_AllocationUsage; this row exists for the relations table's pragmatic edge vocabulary." ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Connection a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Connection" ;
    skos:definition "Connection edge in the semantic layer's relations backbone — an SDG relational flattening of what SysMLv2 reifies as ConnectionUsage (itself a part usage, not an edge kind)." ;
    skos:editorialNote "SDG RELATIONAL FLATTENING (census 2026-07-25: NOT a SysMLv2 metaclass) — the reified form is ConnectionUsage (out-of-set); this row exists for the relations table's pragmatic edge vocabulary." ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_ItemFlow a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "ItemFlow" ;
    skos:definition "Item / material flow edge in the semantic layer's relations backbone — an SDG relational flattening; the current metamodel reifies flows as the Flow / FlowUsage family (the older ItemFlow name has been superseded upstream)." ;
    skos:editorialNote "SDG RELATIONAL FLATTENING (census 2026-07-25: NOT a current metaclass — the metamodel's Flow/FlowDefinition/FlowUsage family superseded the ItemFlow name; version-watch with the scheme)." ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:SysMLv2IntegrationScheme .

sdg:SysMLv2_Dependency a skos:Concept, sdg:SysMLv2Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "Dependency" ;
    skos:definition "Generic dependency between elements." ;
    skos:editorialNote "specializes (census): Relationship" ;
    skos:broader sdg:SysMLv2_Relationship ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.omg.org/spec/KerML/> ;
    skos:inScheme sdg:KerMLScheme .
